---
description: Conventions for run.sh, installer.sh, their Windows twins (run.ps1, installer.ps1, *.cmd) and scripts/
globs: "{*.sh,*.ps1,*.cmd,scripts/**}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Shell scripts

- Bash with `set -euo pipefail`; they must work with macOS's bash 3.2 (no `mapfile`, no `${var,,}`, no
  associative arrays).
- Shared helpers (colours, `die`, `note`, `ask`, `ensure_node`, `ensure_packages`) live in `scripts/common.sh`;
  scripts set `MANAGER_DIR` and `source` it.
- Windows has the same scripts in PowerShell: `run.ps1`, `installer.ps1` and `scripts/common.ps1`, started through
  `run.cmd` and `installer.cmd` (which bypass the execution policy and work by double-click). They take the same options
  as the bash scripts. Keep both sides in step when changing what a script does.
- PowerShell must run in Windows PowerShell 5.1: no `??`, `?:`, `&&`, `||` or `-Parallel`. Native commands run at the
  script level, not inside functions whose result is used, or their output is swallowed. `Get-Item` needs `-Force` for
  dot files.
- `run.sh` and `run.ps1` loop on exit code 75 (the manager restarting after an update) and set `MANAGER_RESTART=1`;
  keep that loop when editing them.
- Packages install with `npm ci` when `package-lock.json` exists, so a git clone stays clean for updates.
- Prompts must have a default and work without a TTY (`--yes`, piped input).
- Never touch anything outside the manager folder and the workspace the user chose; never `sudo`. The one exception is
  the app shortcut (`node src/main.ts --shortcut`, `src/shortcut.ts`), which the installers only add when asked.
- Check syntax after editing: `bash -n run.sh installer.sh scripts/common.sh`; for PowerShell, parse the files with
  `[System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser]::ParseFile` in `pwsh` (a portable build in `/tmp` works).
- Test the installers only on a copy under `/tmp` (`rsync` the repo without `.cache`, `.git`), never in a real
  install, and with `HOME` pointed at a temp folder so a shortcut never lands in the real Applications folder.
